Meeting Assistant original application source is distributed under MIT.

Dependency libraries, inference runtimes, codecs, fonts and model weights retain
their own licenses. The application license does not relicense those components.
Packaging generates actual Python and JavaScript CycloneDX inventories, Cargo
metadata, artifact SHA-256 records and third-party license texts under
artifacts/release. Review the inventories for the actual shipped target.

Optional model/runtime catalog entries must identify upstream revisions,
transformations, artifact checksums, licensing and any acquisition terms.
Gated models are not included in the base application. A user's acquisition
credentials must never be embedded in a runtime package or installer.

Native codec builds require artifact-level redistribution review. A permissive
Python package declaration does not establish the license of bundled FFmpeg,
TorchCodec or other native binary dependencies.

Unicode PDF export embeds ReportLab's bundled Bitstream Vera font. The actual
font and its Bitstream Vera license are included with the engine under
reportlab/fonts/bitstream-vera-license.txt and in generated third-party notices.
This font license is distinct from ReportLab's own library license. Unsupported
glyphs are reported explicitly rather than silently replaced in a PDF.

The vendored tauri-plugin-updater 2.14.0 is public Tauri dependency source,
not original application or company-repository code. Its Apache-2.0/MIT
license files and upstream notices are preserved in its vendor directory.
The only local source change is upgrading its ZIP dependency from 4 to 9
to resolve RUSTSEC-2026-0367, -0368 and -0369. UPSTREAM.json records the
verified crates.io archive hash and upstream revision. The root Cargo.lock
is the sole active lockfile; replace this patch when upstream adopts ZIP 9.
